Design Thinking Case Study
Apparel Production Capacity Planner


Technology Stack: Next.js, React, TypeScript, Supabase, PostgreSQL, Vercel

1. Background

Apparel manufacturing companies receive multiple customer orders every day. Before accepting a new production order, planners must determine whether the selected production line has sufficient capacity to complete the order before its shipment deadline.

Each production line consists of four production departments:

Cut
 ↓
Sew
 ↓
Finish
 ↓
Pack

Each department has a different daily production capacity.

Since production can only move as fast as the slowest department, the effective production capacity of a line is determined by its Bottleneck Department.

Without a production planning system, factories often experience:

Shipment delays
Overloaded production lines
Poor production visibility
Manual spreadsheet-based planning
Difficulty estimating production completion dates
2. Problem Statement

The objective of this Design Thinking case study is to develop a prototype that enables production planners to determine whether a production line can accommodate a new customer order over the next four weeks.

The planning decision is based on:

Production Line Capacity
Incoming Order Quantity
Production Start Date
Shipment Date
Bottleneck Department
Production Completion Date

The application should clearly indicate whether the order can be completed on time or if it will result in a production spillover.

3. Design Thinking Process
Empathize
Primary Users
Production Planner
Factory Manager
Capacity Planning Team
User Pain Points
Difficult to estimate production completion.
Manual capacity calculations.
No visibility into bottlenecks.
Difficult to determine whether an order should be accepted.
Limited visibility into future production capacity.
Define
Problem Statement

How might we help production planners quickly determine whether a production line can accommodate a new order by automatically calculating production capacity, identifying bottlenecks, and visualizing factory availability?

Ideate

The proposed workflow is:

Dashboard
      ↓
Production Planning Form
      ↓
Select Production Line
      ↓
Auto-load Department Capacities
      ↓
Enter Order Details
      ↓
Capacity Calculation
      ↓
Recommendation Popup
      ↓
Capacity Result
      ↓
Production Schedule
      ↓
Recent Production Plans
      ↓
4 Week Capacity Outlook
Prototype

A web application was developed using:

Next.js
React
TypeScript
Supabase
PostgreSQL

The prototype allows users to:

Select a Production Line
Automatically load department capacities
Enter production order details
Calculate effective production capacity
Identify bottlenecks
Estimate production completion date
Detect production spillover
Generate production recommendations
View production schedule
View recent production plans
Visualize factory capacity over four weeks
Test

The application was tested using multiple production scenarios.

The following validations were successfully completed:

Production line retrieved successfully
Department capacities loaded automatically
Bottleneck identified correctly
Effective capacity calculated correctly
Required production days calculated
Completion date estimated
Factory status determined correctly
Spillover detected correctly
Recommendation popup displayed
Production plan stored successfully
Dashboard refreshed automatically
Production schedule updated
Recent production plans refreshed
Four-week capacity outlook updated

4. Solution Overview

The solution consists of six major modules.

Dashboard

Displays:

Factory Status
Production Plans
Production Lines

Provides an overview of the current factory planning status.

Production Planning

Allows users to:

Select Production Line
Enter Style Name
Enter Quantity
Enter Production Start Date
Enter Shipment Date

Department capacities are automatically populated after selecting the production line.

Capacity Calculation Engine

The backend performs the following calculations:

Read selected production line
Identify bottleneck department
Determine effective production capacity
Calculate required production days
Estimate completion date
Compare completion date with shipment date
Determine factory status
Calculate production spillover
Generate production recommendation
Recommendation Popup

After planning an order, the application immediately informs the planner whether the order can be accommodated.

The popup displays:

Order Accepted / Capacity Alert
Production Line
Quantity
Completion Date
Shipment Date
Spillover Days (if applicable)
Production Recommendation
Production Schedule

Displays all planned production orders sorted by production start date.

Four Week Capacity Outlook

Displays the production outlook for:

Week 1
Week 2
Week 3
Week 4

Each week is categorized as:

🟢 AVAILABLE

🟡 NEAR FULL

🔴 FULL

